<%# THE PROJECTS COLUMN (Shop manual spec §7), in two shapes, and ShellHelper#sidebar_current's key
    follows the one on screen.

    ON THE INDEX, the filters the index already understands: All (the live projects) and Archived
    (`?archived=1`), then each kind in use (`?kind=`; ProjectsController#index's `@project_kinds`,
    already loaded for its own chips). Each row is one filter, so the lit one is the filter applied;
    the page's own chips keep combining a kind with a tag or the archive.

    ON ANY OTHER PROJECTS PAGE (a project, its sub-pages, New project), the projects: the eight most
    recently updated live ones (ShellHelper#sidebar_projects, one query), then All projects and New
    project. A project's page lights its row, or All projects when it is older than the eight. A
    project's own contents column is slice 5's, written by the project page. %>
<% if controller_path == "projects" && action_name == "index" %>
  <div class="column-group">
    <h2 class="column-head">Projects</h2>
    <%= column_row "All", projects_path, key: [ :all_projects ] %>
    <%= column_row "Archived", projects_path(archived: 1), key: [ :archived_projects ] %>
  </div>
  <% if Array(@project_kinds).any? %>
    <div class="column-group">
      <h2 class="column-head">Type</h2>
      <% @project_kinds.each do |kind| %>
        <%= column_row Maker::ProjectKind.label(kind), projects_path(kind: kind), key: [ :project_kind, kind ] %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <div class="column-group">
    <h2 class="column-head">Projects</h2>
    <% sidebar_projects.each do |project| %>
      <%= column_row project.name, project_path(project), key: [ :project, project.id ] %>
    <% end %>
    <%= column_row "All projects", projects_path, key: [ :all_projects ] %>
    <%= column_row "New project", new_project_path, key: [ :new_project ] %>
  </div>
<% end %>
